<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-2929] IgniteContext should not have type parameters</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-2929</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Currently implementation of &lt;tt&gt;SparkContext&lt;/tt&gt; has type parameters &lt;tt&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;K, V&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/tt&gt; which means that all the RDDs that are created by a particular instance of context have to be of the same type.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Looks like type parameters on &lt;tt&gt;IgniteContext&lt;/tt&gt; don&apos;t make much sense and should be removed. &lt;tt&gt;fromCache&lt;/tt&gt; method should be parameterized instead.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
        <key id="12955120">IGNITE-2929</key>
            <summary>IgniteContext should not have type parameters</summary>
